## Fix Prompt to Apply

For the System Architect (owner of Word mappings and bindings).

Finding: E2E-001, service mcp-service, check term-mappings — the Then concept `answer` (product.yaml `concepts.then`) uses the term `reply`, declared in the product glossary, but `architecture.terms` has mappings only for `mcp service` and `message`. The term `reply` therefore has no Word mapping.

Fix: add one `architecture.terms` entry for `reply`, using the technical meaning and observation you gave. Nothing in the Scenario, the generated test, or any step definition changes; the product glossary already declares `reply`, so it stays untouched.

File: ./docs/architecture/architecture.yaml

old_string:
    - term: message
      technical: >-
        One JSON-RPC request whose params carry the text, posted to /mcp.
      observed_by: >-
        Post the request to /mcp and keep the response for the steps after.

new_string:
    - term: message
      technical: >-
        One JSON-RPC request whose params carry the text, posted to /mcp.
      observed_by: >-
        Post the request to /mcp and keep the response for the steps after.
    - term: reply
      technical: >-
        The JSON-RPC response body returned by POST /mcp, whose result
        carries the answer text as a string.
      observed_by: >-
        Read the result text out of the response the send step kept, and
        compare it with the stated text.

Why this shape: `term` is the glossary word verbatim (`reply`), `technical` states what the word is in the implementation (the JSON-RPC response body from POST /mcp carrying the answer text), and `observed_by` is prose for how a step definition observes it — reading the result text out of the response the When step kept and comparing it with the stated text, which is what a Then does (observe and compare). All three are nonempty strings and none is a reference object.

No other document needs editing: this is a term-mappings finding, so `architecture.concepts` bindings and the service's Public interface declarations are unaffected.

